
### The Four Gathering Tables
Each Major Action is only available each day through a specific time.
Each is still a Major Action with its own time cost, skill, and DC (see Action System above). Roll a d4 on the relevant table; the result tells you the tier.
All DC 18 = Huge
Half DC 18 = Large
At least one DC 18 = Medium
All below DC 18 = Small
a roll below 10 reduces the gathered stage by 1

The more players in an area the less they can obtain
4 players same area = 2 per gather
3 players same area = 3 per gather
2 players same area = 4 per gather
1 players same area = 5 per gather

**Forage Table — d4**

| d4 | Tier | Item | Slots | Base Value |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Small | Herb sprig | 1 | 2gp |
| 2 | Medium | Wild berries / fever root | 2 | 5gp |
| 3 | Large | River clay bundle / nightbloom cluster | 3 | 9gp |
| 4 | Huge | Rare specimen / Serpent's Tongue | 5 | 18gp (Soren-assessed, 15-30gp range) |

Wisdom (Survival): The trek. Navigating the deep brush of the Forest Edge to locate the specific micro-climates where the gathering nodes actually grow.
Wisdom (Perception): The search. Scanning the undergrowth to spot camouflaged items, like river clay banks or hidden nightblooms.
Intelligence (Nature): The verification. Examining the found plants to ensure they are the safe, usable variants before picking them.
Wisdom (Medicine): The extraction. Carefully cutting and harvesting the herbs without destroying the delicate roots, stems, or medicinal properties.

**Hunt Table — d4**

| d4 | Tier | Item | Slots | Base Value |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Small | Small game (meat + pelt) | 1 | 3gp |
| 2 | Medium | Wild fowl (meat + feathers) | 2 | 6gp |
| 3 | Large | Boar or deer (meat + hide, +antler if deer) | 3 | 12gp |
| 4 | Huge | Dangerous prey — Athletics DC 16 or 2d8 damage, catch lost on fail | 5 | 24gp |

Wisdom (Survival): The pursuit. Tracking footprints, scat, and broken branches to find where the game is moving or bedding down.
Intelligence (Nature): The ambush. Knowing the watering holes, feeding grounds, and behavior patterns of the local game to set up a blind.
Wisdom (Animal Handling): The trap. Masking human scent and setting physical snares, lures, or bait lines in a way that naturally manipulates the beast without spooking it.
Dexterity (Stealth): The approach. Creeping through the dense Forest Edge to get a clean, unnoticed strike on the prey.

**Fish Table — d4**

| d4 | Tier | Item | Slots | Base Value |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Small | Common fish ×3 | 1 | 3gp |
| 2 | Medium | River trout ×2 | 2 | 6gp |
| 3 | Large | Large pike | 3 | 10gp |
| 4 | Huge | Luminous eel | 5 | 20gp |

Intelligence (Nature): The read. Analyzing the river currents, tides, and depths to understand where the deep-water drop-offs and fish populations are.
Wisdom (Survival): The preparation. Sourcing the right local bait and knowing exactly what time of day the river trout or pike are biting.
Wisdom (Perception): The stakeout. Staring intently at the water to spot the subtle shadows of a large catch or the faint glow of a luminous eel beneath the surface.
Dexterity (Sleight of Hand): The catch. The precise, split-second wrist flick required to set the hook before the fish steals the bait, or snagging it bare-handed.

**Mine Table — d4 (Underground only)**

| d4 | Tier | Item | Slots | Base Value |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Small | Common stone | 1 | 2gp |
| 2 | Medium | Copper ore | 2 | 6gp |
| 3 | Large | Iron ore | 3 | 10gp |
| 4 | Huge | Quartzite crystal | 5 | 20gp |


Intelligence (Nature): The scout. Reading the geological strata and rock formations of the cellar tunnels to locate where natural ore veins form.
Wisdom (Perception): The spot. Catching the faint glint of valuable minerals or quartzite crystal in the dark, torch-lit tunnels.
Intelligence (Investigation): The analysis. Tapping the rock face and studying the fissures to find the exact structural weak points.
Strength (Athletics): The strike. The sheer physical power and endurance required to break hard stone with a pickaxe and extract the ore intact.

**Warning:** each Mining trip carries a 1-in-6 chance of a Syndicate Enforcer encounter unless a Stealth DC 13 check is made before descending.


